<header class="profile" id="top">
  <div>
    <h1>Yanlin Wang <span lang="zh-CN">王焱林</span></h1>
    <p>Associate Professor and PhD Supervisor, School of Software Engineering, Sun Yat-sen University</p>
    <p>My research on large language models, agents and trustworthy AI explores how intelligent systems can reason, remember, use tools and collaborate autonomously in settings such as software engineering, question answering and embodied interaction.</p>
    <p class="meta">I received my bachelor's degree from Zhejiang University and my PhD in computer science from the University of Hong Kong, advised by <a href="https://i.cs.hku.hk/~bruno/">Bruno C. d. S. Oliveira</a>. At Microsoft (2019–2022), my research mentors were <a href="https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/people/dongmeiz/">Dongmei Zhang</a> and <a href="https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/people/shihan/">Shi Han</a>. I joined Sun Yat-sen University in 2022.</p>
<p>Email: <a href="mailto:yanlin-wang@outlook.com">yanlin-wang@outlook.com</a></p>
<p>Other：<a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?hl=en&amp;user=xSCoImAAAAAJ">Google Scholar</a> (9,532 citations)　<a href="https://sse.sysu.edu.cn/teacher/329">Faculty profile (Chinese)</a>　<a href="https://dblp.org/pid/41/3458-1.html">DBLP</a>　<a href="https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7761-7269">ORCID</a></p>
