<section class="section-block" id="research">
  <h2>Research interests</h2>
  <article class="direction" id="agents">
    <img alt="" class="direction-art" height="80" src="pic/research/agents.webp" width="80"/>
    <div class="direction-text">
      <h3>LLM Agents and Autonomous Learning</h3>
      <ul class="topic-list">
        <li>
          <strong class="subtopic">Memory, collaboration and repair</strong>
          <a aria-label="MemoryBank: Enhancing Large Language Models with Long-Term Memory (AAAI'24)" class="short-ref" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.10250" title="MemoryBank: Enhancing Large Language Models with Long-Term Memory (AAAI'24)">[MemoryBank, AAAI'24]</a>
          <a aria-label="MAGIS: LLM-Based Multi-Agent Framework for GitHub Issue Resolution (NeurIPS'24)" class="short-ref" href="https://doi.org/10.52202/079017-1647" title="MAGIS: LLM-Based Multi-Agent Framework for GitHub Issue Resolution (NeurIPS'24)">[MAGIS, NeurIPS'24]</a>
          <a aria-label="MicroAgent: Context-Augmented Multi-agent Framework for Automatic Microservice Decomposition (ASE'26)" class="short-ref" href="https://doi.org/10.1145/3832783.3834441" title="MicroAgent: Context-Augmented Multi-agent Framework for Automatic Microservice Decomposition (ASE'26)">[MicroAgent, ASE'26]</a>
          <a aria-label="AdverIntent-Agent: Adversarial Reasoning for Repair Based on Inferred Program Intent (ISSTA'25)" class="short-ref" href="https://doi.org/10.1145/3728939" title="AdverIntent-Agent: Adversarial Reasoning for Repair Based on Inferred Program Intent (ISSTA'25)">[AdverIntent-Agent, ISSTA'25]</a>
          <a aria-label="PhoenixRepair: Rethinking Repair Strategy Exploration in Software Agents (arXiv'26)" class="short-ref" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.18859" title="PhoenixRepair: Rethinking Repair Strategy Exploration in Software Agents (arXiv'26)">[PhoenixRepair, arXiv'26]</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="subtopic">Repository-level generation and retrieval</strong>
          <a aria-label="RLCoder: Reinforcement Learning for Repository-Level Code Completion (ICSE'25)" class="short-ref" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.19487" title="RLCoder: Reinforcement Learning for Repository-Level Code Completion (ICSE'25)">[RLCoder, ICSE'25]</a>
          <a aria-label="AlignCoder: Aligning Retrieval with Target Intent for Repository-Level Code Completion (ASE'25)" class="short-ref" href="https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2025/ase-2025-papers/34/AlignCoder-Aligning-Retrieval-with-Target-Intent-for-Repository-Level-Code-Completio" title="AlignCoder: Aligning Retrieval with Target Intent for Repository-Level Code Completion (ASE'25)">[AlignCoder, ASE'25]</a>
          <a aria-label="RepoMinCoder: Improving Repository-Level Code Generation Based on Information Loss Screening (Internetware'24)" class="short-ref" href="https://doi.org/10.1145/3671016.3674819" title="RepoMinCoder: Improving Repository-Level Code Generation Based on Information Loss Screening (Internetware'24)">[RepoMinCoder, Internetware'24]</a>
          <a aria-label="From Logical to Computational Sparsity: Structure-Aware Block-Sparse Attention for Long-Code Completion (ACL'26)" class="short-ref" href="https://aclanthology.org/2026.acl-long.1189/" title="From Logical to Computational Sparsity: Structure-Aware Block-Sparse Attention for Long-Code Completion (ACL'26)">[SabreCoder, ACL'26]</a>
          <a aria-label="Adaptive Critical Token-Aware Retrieval for Repository-Level Code Generation (arXiv'26)" class="short-ref" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.01601" title="Adaptive Critical Token-Aware Retrieval for Repository-Level Code Generation (arXiv'26)">[ACToR, arXiv'26]</a>
          <a aria-label="WebDesignIter: Co-Evolving Design Knowledge for Repository-Level Front-End Code Generation (arXiv'26)" class="short-ref" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.10621" title="WebDesignIter: Co-Evolving Design Knowledge for Repository-Level Front-End Code Generation (arXiv'26)">[WebDesignIter, arXiv'26]</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="subtopic">Learning from experience and training agents</strong>
          <a aria-label="SWE Data Construction, Automatically! (FSE'26)" class="short-ref" href="https://doi.org/10.1145/3797119" title="SWE Data Construction, Automatically! (FSE'26)">[SWE-Factory, FSE'26]</a>
          <a aria-label="SWE-Prime: Fewer Trajectories, Better Performance (arXiv'26)" class="short-ref" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.27449" title="SWE-Prime: Fewer Trajectories, Better Performance (arXiv'26)">[SWE-Prime, arXiv'26]</a>
          <a aria-label="EvoGuard: Mitigating Degradation in Online Skill Evolution (arXiv'26)" class="short-ref" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.06444" title="EvoGuard: Mitigating Degradation in Online Skill Evolution (arXiv'26)">[EvoGuard, arXiv'26]</a>
          <a aria-label="RSI-Prime: Training Models to Train Models (arXiv'26)" class="short-ref" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.23138" title="RSI-Prime: Training Models to Train Models (arXiv'26)">[RSI-Prime, arXiv'26]</a>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </article>
  <article class="direction" id="trustworthy-models">
    <img alt="" class="direction-art" height="80" src="pic/research/evaluation.webp" width="80"/>
    <div class="direction-text">
      <h3>LLM Training, Evaluation, Trustworthiness and Safety</h3>
      <ul class="topic-list">
        <li>
          <strong class="subtopic">Code representations and training</strong>
          <a aria-label="UniXcoder: Unified Cross-Modal Pre-training for Code Representation (ACL'22)" class="short-ref" href="https://aclanthology.org/2022.acl-long.499/" title="UniXcoder: Unified Cross-Modal Pre-training for Code Representation (ACL'22)">[UniXcoder, ACL'22]</a>
          <a aria-label="CoCoSoDa: Effective Contrastive Learning for Code Search (ICSE'23)" class="short-ref" href="https://dl.acm.org/doi/abs/10.1109/ICSE48619.2023.00185" title="CoCoSoDa: Effective Contrastive Learning for Code Search (ICSE'23)">[CoCoSoDa, ICSE'23]</a>
          <a aria-label="YODA: Teacher-Student Progressive Learning for Language Models (arXiv'24)" class="short-ref" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2401.15670" title="YODA: Teacher-Student Progressive Learning for Language Models (arXiv'24)">[YODA, arXiv'24]</a>
          <a aria-label="Large Language Models Are Qualified Benchmark Builders: Rebuilding Pre-Training Datasets for Advancing Code Intelligence Tasks (ICPC'25)" class="short-ref" href="https://doi.org/10.1109/ICPC66645.2025.00038" title="Large Language Models Are Qualified Benchmark Builders: Rebuilding Pre-Training Datasets for Advancing Code Intelligence Tasks (ICPC'25)">[Benchmark Builders, ICPC'25]</a>
          <a aria-label="Towards Better Code Understanding in Decoder-Only Models with Contrastive Learning (AAAI'26)" class="short-ref" href="https://doi.org/10.1609/aaai.v40i38.40471" title="Towards Better Code Understanding in Decoder-Only Models with Contrastive Learning (AAAI'26)">[CL4D, AAAI'26]</a>
          <a aria-label="EffiReasonTrans: RL-Optimized Reasoning for Code Translation (TSE'26)" class="short-ref" href="https://doi.org/10.1109/tse.2026.3693795" title="EffiReasonTrans: RL-Optimized Reasoning for Code Translation (TSE'26)">[EffiReasonTrans, TSE'26]</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="subtopic">Capability and process evaluation</strong>
          <a aria-label="AGIEval: A Human-Centric Benchmark for Evaluating Foundation Models (NAACL Findings'24)" class="short-ref" href="https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2024.findings-naacl.149" title="AGIEval: A Human-Centric Benchmark for Evaluating Foundation Models (NAACL Findings'24)">[AGIEval, NAACL Findings'24]</a>
          <a aria-label="Top General Performance = Top Domain Performance? DomainCodeBench: A Multi-domain Code Generation Benchmark (ICSE'26)" class="short-ref" href="https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2026/icse-2026-research-track/229/Top-General-Performance-Top-Domain-Performance-DomainCodeBench-A-Multi-domain-Cod" title="Top General Performance = Top Domain Performance? DomainCodeBench: A Multi-domain Code Generation Benchmark (ICSE'26)">[DomainCodeBench, ICSE'26]</a>
          <a aria-label="From Conversation to Evaluation: Benchmarking LLMs on Development Knowledge via SimpleDevQA (ACL Findings'26)" class="short-ref" href="https://aclanthology.org/2026.findings-acl.1877/" title="From Conversation to Evaluation: Benchmarking LLMs on Development Knowledge via SimpleDevQA (ACL Findings'26)">[SimpleDevQA, ACL Findings'26]</a>
          <a aria-label="RepoReasoner: Evaluating Repository-Level Code Reasoning Ability of Long-Context Language Models (FSE'26)" class="short-ref" href="https://doi.org/10.1145/3808131" title="RepoReasoner: Evaluating Repository-Level Code Reasoning Ability of Long-Context Language Models (FSE'26)">[RepoReasoner, FSE'26]</a>
          <a aria-label="From Static to Dynamic: Benchmarking Real-World Code Review with MCR-Bench (ISSTA'26)" class="short-ref" href="https://doi.org/10.1145/3832219" title="From Static to Dynamic: Benchmarking Real-World Code Review with MCR-Bench (ISSTA'26)">[MCR-Bench, ISSTA'26]</a>
          <a aria-label="Efficient SWE Agent Benchmarking via Trajectory-Aware Evaluation (arXiv'26)" class="short-ref" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.01603" title="Efficient SWE Agent Benchmarking via Trajectory-Aware Evaluation (arXiv'26)">[PTA-IRT, arXiv'26]</a>
          <a aria-label="FeedbackEval: A Benchmark for Evaluating Large Language Models in Feedback-Driven Code Repair Tasks (arXiv'25)" class="short-ref" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.06939" title="FeedbackEval: A Benchmark for Evaluating Large Language Models in Feedback-Driven Code Repair Tasks (arXiv'25)">[FeedbackEval, arXiv'25]</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="subtopic">Code reliability and security</strong>
          <a aria-label="LLM Hallucinations in Practical Code Generation: Phenomena, Mechanism, and Mitigation (ISSTA'25)" class="short-ref" href="https://doi.org/10.1145/3728894" title="LLM Hallucinations in Practical Code Generation: Phenomena, Mechanism, and Mitigation (ISSTA'25)">[Code Hallucinations, ISSTA'25]</a>
          <a aria-label="Beyond Functional Correctness: Investigating Coding Style Inconsistencies in Large Language Models (FSE'25)" class="short-ref" href="https://doi.org/10.1145/3715749" title="Beyond Functional Correctness: Investigating Coding Style Inconsistencies in Large Language Models (FSE'25)">[Coding Style, FSE'25]</a>
          <a aria-label="RMCBench: Benchmarking Large Language Models’ Resistance to Malicious Code (ASE'24)" class="short-ref" href="https://doi.org/10.1145/3691620.3695480" title="RMCBench: Benchmarking Large Language Models’ Resistance to Malicious Code (ASE'24)">[RMCBench, ASE'24]</a>
          <a aria-label="RealSec-bench: A Benchmark for Evaluating Secure Code Generation in Real-World Repositories (ACL Findings'26)" class="short-ref" href="https://aclanthology.org/2026.findings-acl.1786/" title="RealSec-bench: A Benchmark for Evaluating Secure Code Generation in Real-World Repositories (ACL Findings'26)">[RealSec-bench, ACL Findings'26]</a>
          <a aria-label="MCGMark: An Encodable and Robust Online Watermark for Tracing LLM-Generated Malicious Code (TOSEM'26)" class="short-ref" href="https://doi.org/10.1145/3846177" title="MCGMark: An Encodable and Robust Online Watermark for Tracing LLM-Generated Malicious Code (TOSEM'26)">[MCGMark, TOSEM'26]</a>
          <a aria-label="SWE-Gate: Passing Functional Tests Is Not Enough for Software Engineering Agents (arXiv'26)" class="short-ref" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.04167" title="SWE-Gate: Passing Functional Tests Is Not Enough for Software Engineering Agents (arXiv'26)">[SWE-Gate, arXiv'26]</a>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </article>
